 
 1. install npm

2. alert('Hello World'); usied in console of browser only.
console.log(`Hello World`); used in node js environment.
3. Data types in JavaScript:
	 - Number
	 - String
	 - Boolean
	 - Undefined
	 - Null
	 - Symbol
	 - BigInt
4. Arrays in JavaScript:
	 - Arrays are used to store multiple values in a single variable.
	 - Arrays are dynamic in size and can hold elements of different data types.
	 - Common array methods include push(), pop(), shift(), unshift(), and length property.
5. To run a JavaScript file using Node.js, use the command: node filename.js
6. To run a JavaScript file in the browser, include it in an HTML file using the <script> tag and open the HTML file in a web browser.


